course: dictionary
lesson: 7299
title: Pistol: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can mean different things, and the context tells you which meaning the writer wants. A pistol is a small gun that you hold and fire with one hand. «At dusk the Rat dresses everybody for the expedition: a belt, a sword, a cutlass, a pair of pistols...» The list of other weapons and a dangerous trip tells you the pistols are weapons.
explain: Other kinds of pistol are toys or sports equipment. A starting pistol only makes a loud bang, and it is used to start races on sports day. A water pistol is a toy that squirts water. To check your meaning, put it into the sentence. Does a bang fit the race? Then the starting pistol is right.
explain: Safety comes first. A real pistol is dangerous. If you ever find a gun, do not touch it, leave the place and tell an adult straight away.
fact: A pistol is a small gun that you hold and fire with one hand.
fact: A starting pistol is a toy-like pistol that only makes a loud bang, used to start races.
fact: A water pistol is a toy that squirts water.
fact: Context clues, the words around a word, show you which meaning is meant.
fact: If you find a real gun, do not touch it: leave the place and tell an adult.
exercise: Badger says, «we shan't want any swords or pistols.» What is a pistol here? | A long, thin fishing rod | A kind of bird | *A small gun that you hold and fire with one hand | A large boat with sails
exercise: On sports day, a starting pistol is used for what? | *To start races with a loud bang | To squirt water over the crowd | To lock the gates | To cook the lunch
exercise: Which of these is a toy that squirts water? | *A water pistol | A policeman's truncheon | A starting pistol | A real pistol
test: If you find a real gun, what should you do? | Hide it in your bag | Fire it into the air | Pick it up to look closely | *Leave the place and tell an adult
test: The Rat packs a sword, a cutlass and a pair of pistols for an expedition. What does this suggest? | That the pistols are for cooking | That the pistols are used only for a race | *That the pistols are weapons for a dangerous adventure | That the pistols are toys for a picnic
exam: «The pistol cracked at the start line and the runners sprinted off.» What was the pistol? | A small fish that snaps its claw | *A starting pistol that makes a loud bang | A toy that squirts water | A pair of handcuffs
